// Texts GZH Neo adds to the game (English). Format as in EA's map.str files: label, quoted text, END.
// The game loads ProjectData\Text\<language>.str and falls back to this file.

GZH:LanErrorVersion
"The host runs a different version of the game. All players need the same version."
END

GZH:LanErrorData
"Your game data differs from the host's, for example because of another mod or changed INI files."
END

GZH:LanVersionDetail
"Host: %ls, network protocol %u\nYou: %ls, network protocol %u"
END

GZH:DirectConnectBadAddress
"Please enter an IP address (for example 192.168.0.10 or 2001:db8::10) or a host name, without a port."
END

GZH:DirectConnectNoIPv6
"This computer has no IPv6 connection. Please enter an IPv4 address or a host name."
END

GZH:DirectConnectNotFound
"No address was found for this host name."
END

GZH:LanGameKeyHost
"Game key: %hs. It holds no address: players who join over the internet type the address of this computer together with the key (address#%hs)."
END

GZH:LanGameKeyJoined
"Game key of the host: %hs. Compare it with the host to rule out that someone sits in between (%hs)."
END

GZH:LanErrorHostKey
"The host's game key does not match the key you typed. Someone may sit in between; the join was cancelled."
END

GZH:DirectConnectBadCode
"The game key after # has the form K7Q2-9XPA."
END

GZH:LanGameOtherVersion
"(other version)"
END

GZH:LanGameOtherData
"(other game data)"
END

GZH:LanPortsNoRouter
"Router: no router answered UPnP or NAT-PMP; IPv4 ports %u and %u stay as they are. If you forwarded them to this computer by hand, you can ignore this."
END

GZH:LanPortsRefused
"Router: the router refused to open IPv4 ports %u and %u (UPnP error %d). On a FRITZ!Box, allow 'permit independent port sharing' for this computer. If you forwarded the ports by hand, you can ignore this."
END

GZH:LanNoPublicIPv4
"Router: your connection has no public IPv4 address of its own (the router reports %hs, as with DS-Lite). Nobody on the internet reaches you over IPv4, not even with port forwarding; players on the internet join over IPv6."
END

GZH:LanInternetJoinV6
"Over IPv6, players on the internet join by Direct Connect with %hs#%hs. The router must let incoming UDP %u and %u through to this computer (IPv6 port sharing; the game asks the router for it over UPnP, the router line tells whether that worked)."
END

GZH:LanJoinCopied
"Copied to the clipboard to pass on: %ls"
END

GZH:LanNoAnswer
"The host does not answer. Most often its router keeps the connection out: for IPv6 it must allow incoming UDP %u and %u to the host's computer, for IPv4 forward these ports to it. With DS-Lite only IPv6 works."
END

GZH:DirectConnectKeyOnly
"That is only the game key; it holds no address. Please type the host's address together with the key, such as [2001:db8::7]#K7Q2-9XPA or 203.0.113.5#K7Q2-9XPA. The host finds both in the chat of the game and on the clipboard."
END

GZH:LanPinholesOpen
"Router: the IPv6 firewall lets UDP %u and %u through to this computer (UPnP)."
END

GZH:LanPinholesNotNeeded
"Router: its IPv6 firewall is off; players reach this computer directly over IPv6."
END

GZH:LanPinholesNoService
"Router: it offers no IPv6 port sharing over UPnP. For games over IPv6, allow incoming UDP %u and %u to this computer in the router."
END

GZH:LanPinholesRefused
"Router: it refused the IPv6 port sharing for UDP %u and %u (UPnP error %d). On a FRITZ!Box, allow 'permit independent port sharing' for this computer; otherwise set it up in the router by hand."
END

GZH:LanRouterLog
"Router: the details of the port forwarding (which routers answered and what they said) are in %hs. This file helps to find the cause."
END

GZH:PlayerReturned
"%ls is back in the game."
END

GZH:ReturnClosed
"%ls can no longer come back; their units are gone."
END

GZH:ReturnComing
"%ls is coming back into the game and catching up."
END

GZH:ReturnJoined
"Back into the running game: catching up with it."
END

GZH:ReturnBack
"You are back in the game."
END

GZH:ReturnRefused
"The host did not take you back into the game."
END

GZH:ReturnLost
"The host no longer answers; the way back into the game is lost."
END

GZH:ReturnLostBeforeStart
"The game could not be started again."
END

GZH:ReturnOffer
"A game of %ls may still be running and take you back if you were dropped from it: type /return."
END

GZH:ReturnNone
"There is no game to go back into."
END

GZH:WatchStarted
"%ls is watching the game now."
END

GZH:WatchStopped
"%ls stopped watching."
END

GZH:WatchJoined
"The game is already running: you are watching. It loads and catches up in fast motion."
END

GZH:WatchLost
"The game's stream broke off; what arrived until then is shown."
END

GZH:WatchLostBeforeStart
"The game's stream broke off before it could begin."
END

GZH:WatchNoMap
"Cannot watch: the game's map is missing on this computer (spectators get no map transfer)."
END

GZH:LanSearchFiltered
"Router: UPnP is on in the router, but its answers to the search did not arrive on this computer. Most likely a firewall drops them (Windows Firewall or a virus scanner). The game therefore asked the router directly."
END

GZH:LanUpnpOff
"Router: neither the UPnP search nor the usual addresses of the router answer. UPnP is probably off in the router."
END

GZH:LanPortsOpened
"Router: UDP ports %u and %u are forwarded to this computer (%hs)."
END

GZH:LanInternetAddress
"Your address on the internet: %hs"
END

GZH:LanInternetJoin
"Players on the internet join by Direct Connect with %hs#%hs"
END

GZH:DesyncReport
"The games of the players have drifted apart. A report for the developers was saved: %ls"
END

GZH:LanInvite
"Invitation code for players on the internet: %hs (Direct Connect, address field)"
END

GZH:LanInviteNone
"No rendezvous server answered; players on the internet join by address."
END

GZH:LanErrorNotFound
"No rendezvous server knows this invitation code. The host may have left, or the code is mistyped."
END

